hypotheses.statement:
For every fixed $v\ne0$, $$\label{eq:sign-union}
 P_0(A_v)>0\quad\Longrightarrow\quad
 p_v>0\ \text{ and }\ P_0(A_v\cup A_{-v})=1.$$ More precisely, when $p_v>0$, infinite height supremum implies $A_v$ almost surely, and finite height supremum implies $A_{-v}$ almost surely.

Let $v
e0$ satisfy $\|v\|_\infty=1$. If $P_0(A_v)>0$ and $P_0(A_{-v})>0$, then the regeneration-word laws of Proposition <a href="#prop:cut-law" data-reference-type="ref" data-reference="prop:cut-law">3</a> satisfy $$E_{
u_v}\mathcal R+E_{
u_{-v}}\mathcal R<\infty.
  \label{eq:radius-moment}$$

Assume $p_+p_->0$, and let $M\le k<r<N$ be integers with $r-k\ge R$. Start a positive bridge $Y$ with law $\mathcal B_N^+$ at the origin, and put $E_{\mathrm{lat}}=\pi Y_{T_N}$. Independently of $Y$, sample a relative marked path with law $\widehat P_-$, and translate it to start at $(N-1,E_{\mathrm{lat}})$; denote the resulting path by $\beta$. Define $$\tau=\inf\{i:T_k(Y)\le i<T_N(Y),\quad
       \|Y_i-\beta_j\|_\infty\le R\text{ for some }j\ge0\},$$ with $\inf\varnothing=\infty$. Let $$\label{eq:first-contact-event}
 \mathcal C_{k,r,N}=
 \left\{
 \begin{gathered}
  \mathcal D_k^+(Y),\quad \tau<T_N(Y),\quad (Y_\tau)_1\ge r,\\
  \min_{T_k(Y)\le i\le\tau}(Y_i)_1\ge k,
  \quad |E_{\mathrm{lat}}|\le N^2
 \end{gathered}
 \right\}.$$ Here $\mathcal D_k^+(Y)$ is a condition on the prefix through the first hit of $k$. There is a constant $C$, independent of $k,r,N$, such that, with $\Delta=u_{r-k}^+-u_{N-k}^+$, $$\label{eq:first-contact-bound}
 P(\mathcal C_{k,r,N})
 \le C\log(2N)\,\Delta\log^2(\mathrm e/\Delta).$$ The right-hand side is defined to be zero when $\Delta=0$.

